== TWOUSE (A3): an argument the body uses both alone and labelled: the two candidates differ in ANSWER
PASS TWOUSE: `B(A) & (A.d: <5)`, B(rx) := `/${[p = rx]}-${rx}/`: (local) reads the alone use (the second digit), differing 0; (error) reads `p`'s (the first digit), differing 0, over 40 texts
