PASS SETAND: `B & (B.a: 9)`, B := `A & /(?<a>\d)/` (a pattern; its literal's `a` exported): differing 0; the program `B`, B := `A & A`, matching one digit: differing 0
== VISIBLE (E2): a read of a label not visible where it is written: inside a body, and a BARE name at the top
PASS VISIBLE: inside C `B.h` refused True; at the top the bare `g` of an argument the body uses alone, under (error), refused True; `B.A.h` through B's part label legal True
